<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muzaffar Shah I of Perak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1549</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaffar-shah-i">Muzaffar Shah I</a> was the first sultan of Perak, reigning from about 1528 to 1549. The eldest son of Mahmud Shah, the last sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>, he was passed over for the succession in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> and invited to rule Perak, founding the dynasty that still reigns there. The sultanate grew rich on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> of the Perak valley.</p></div>
